The Table \ref{tab:Sphere_deformation} presents the reconstruction of a unit Sphere from level sets. We performed 100 iterations, both excluding and including the tangential component in our model. The initial surface $\Gamma_{0}$ is a Sphere with a radius of 2. It is evident that with each iteration, the initial surface deforms towards the ideal surface, and the color distribution in each triangle is based on curvature, where red represents high curvature and blue represents low curvature. By the 100th iteration, the curvature of the Sphere is nearly $1$. The fourth column represents the deformation of the unit Sphere with noisy data, demonstrating the effectiveness of our model even in the presence of noise. Similarly the Table \ref{tab:Ellipsoid}, \ref{tab:Fused Sphere}, \ref{tab:Cylinder} show the reconstruction of Ellipsoid, Fused Sphere and Cylinder from level set, and Tables \ref{tab:marching_cube} represents the reconstruction of the same phantoms using the Marching Cube Method (MCM) as discussed in section \ref{Intro}.


