\section{Conclusion}
\label{sec:Conclusion}

We presented two Gaussian graphical models on complete bipartite graphs, and 
demonstrated that the ratio of the determinants of their precision matrices only 
depends on model parameters.
This equivalence reduces the complexity of computing the exact 
determinant of large precision matrices. Furthermore, it allows the derivation of 
closed-form expressions for the determinants in certain special cases, such as homogeneous models and star graphs.



