\begin{abstract}
    In this paper, we, as the DS@GT team for CLEF 2025 CheckThat! Task 4a Scientific Web Discourse Detection \cite{clef-checkthat:2025:task4}, present the methods we explored for this task. For this multiclass classification task, we determined if a tweet contained a scientific claim, a reference to a scientific study or publication, and/or mentions of scientific entities, such as a university or a scientist. We present 3 modeling approaches for this task: transformer finetuning, few-shot prompting of LLMs, and a combined ensemble model whose design was informed by earlier experiments. Our team placed 7th in the competition, achieving a macro-averaged F1 score of 0.8611, an improvement over the \textit{DeBERTaV3} baseline of 0.8375. Our code is available on Github at \url{https://github.com/dsgt-arc/checkthat-2025-swd/tree/main/subtask-4a}.
\end{abstract}

