\section{Conclusions}
%Summary of the work and its contributions.

\hspace{4pt} In this paper, we discuss 3 approaches for Subtask 4a for CLEF 2025 related to scientific web discourse detection. In particular, we discussed model finetuning, LLM approaches, and a combined model that took the best of both worlds. Our best model beats the baseline \textit{DeBERTaV3} model on macro-average F1 score with a score of 0.86 versus 0.84 for the baseline on the set. We also beat the baseline on categories 1 and 2 as well with F1 scores of 0.86 and 0.85, respectively. 

