{To encode $\mathbf{H}$ using spherical harmonics, we first establish a bijective mapping between the coordinates $(x, y)$ in $\mathbf{H}$ and the spherical coordinates $(\theta, \phi)$. However, the north and south poles in spherical coordinates correspond to singularities, where the azimuthal angle $\phi$ becomes undefined due to all meridians converging at a single point. As a result, these poles do not preserve a one-to-one mapping. To avoid this issue and maintain bijectivity, we define the following adjusted coordinate transformation:}
\begin{equation}
