Additionally, as $\omega$ increases, our completeness, L1-Chamfer distance, and F-score improve, which is expected. This indicates that our map covers more regions of the ground-truth map. The reconstructed maps corresponding to different $\omega$ settings in TABLE \ref{tab:continuous reconstruction}(a) are visualized in Fig. \ref{fig:continuous reconstruction}.

