{The proposed scheduling and configuration policy differs marginally from the best possible results achieved under an error-free channel.} This is because our device selection and adaptive coefficient adjustment take into account time-varying errors from DP, quantization, and transmission, and minimize the maximum of the convergence upper bound among the clients, reducing the impact from DP and noisy channels. The accuracy first increases and then decreases as $T_0$ grows, and the maximum test loss of all participating clients first decreases and then increases for WPFL under the proposed policy {running in either noisy or error-free channels}, due to the accumulated impact of the DP noise.

