\section{Limitations}
Since our dynamic calibration is based on Assum.~\ref{assump:Short-term Static Assumption} and Assum.~\ref{assump:Short-term Diversity Assumption}, it may fail under the following conditions: i) large and sudden changes in $R_{G^{'}G}$ and $R_{BS}$ (e.g., extreme environmental changes or sensor hardware inconsistencies); ii) low-activity scenarios, such as office work, watching TV, etc, where the rotation diversity may not meet the requirement for effective calibration; iii) we only consider the coordinate drift in the ego-yaw frame and do not support the correction of global yaw drift (Fig.~\ref{fig:trans comp}); \revision{iv) irregular motions may lead to incorrect calibration (Fig.~\ref{fig:irregular demo})}.

