\section{Rationale of ego-yaw coordinate system}
We define the ego-yaw coordinate system as the global coordinate system \( G \) in dynamic calibration due to the exist of unresolved components in the drifted foundational world coordinate systems $W^{'}$ (e.g. ENU or SMPL). As illustrated in Fig.~\ref{fig:ego-yaw}, the overall coordinate drift $R_{W^{'}G}$ can be decomposed into two parts: $R_{W^{'}G^{'}}$, corresponding to yaw rotation between drifted ego-yaw and drifted world coordinate system, which is yaw-only rotation that cannot not result in any unnatural motion; thus, it cannot be perceived and resolved through observation. In contrast, the remaining $R_{G^{'}G}$ directly impacts the rotation of human joints, leading to unnatural movements. Therefore, we set  $R_{G^{'}G}$ as the target of dynamic calibration.
