\subsection{Resolution of discretized Euler angle space}
The ideal discretized Euler angle space should use the lowest possible split step to achieve higher resolution and accurately represent rotation diversity. However, since the Euler angle space is three-dimensional, too high a resolution would greatly increase the computational complexity of $RD$ calculation. Therefore, we use a 15-degree split step for discretization, which ensures uniform segmentation with an acceptable $RD$ computation complexity (takes 2.5ms to process 256 frames data on an NVDIA RTX 4080 GPU).


