\section{Reproducibility Test}
The use of randomly generated samples $R_{G^{'}G}$ and $R_{BS}$ in TIC Network training introduces additional uncertainty into the model training process, making reproducibility analysis essential. We performed 10 independent trainings of the TIC Network under a unified training setup and recorded the average OME and AME. As shown in Table~\ref{tab:reproducibility}, the performance variations across the 10 independent model trainings were minimal, indicating that the achieved metrics (OME: 15.20, AME: 1.30) are highly reproducible.

